{"name":"Worn Jade Tiles","hex":"#d4ded4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"worn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Damaged and shabby as a result of much use.","Worn out; exhausted."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of wear"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worn"},{"term":"jade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A semiprecious stone, either nephrite or jadeite, generally green or white in color, often used for carving figurines.","A bright shade of slightly bluish or greyish green, typical of polished jade stones."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a grayish shade of green, typical of jade stones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jade"},{"term":"tiles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tile"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of tile"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wear","blocks":[{"text":"Wear is the damaging, gradual removal or deformation of material at solid surfaces. Causes of wear can be mechanical or chemical. The study of wear and related processes is referred to as tribology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/K%C3%A6detandhjul.jpg/330px-K%C3%A6detandhjul.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wear"},{"title":"Jade","blocks":[{"text":"Jade is an umbrella term for two different types of decorative rocks used for jewelry or ornaments. Jade is often referred to by either of two different silicate mineral names: nephrite, or jadeite. Nephrite is typically green, although it may be yellow, white or black. Jadeite varies from white or near-colorless, through various shades of green, to lavender, yellow, orange, brown and black. Rarely it may be blue. Both of these names refer to their use as gemstones, and each has a mineralogically more specific name. Both the amphibole jade (nephrite) and pyroxene jade are mineral aggregates (rocks) rather than mineral species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Jadestein.jpg/330px-Jadestein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade"},{"title":"Tile","blocks":[{"text":"Tiles are usually thin, square rectangular coverings manufactured from hard-wearing material such as ceramic, stone, metal, baked clay, or even glass. They are generally fixed in place in an array to cover roofs, floors, walls, edges, or other objects such as tabletops. Alternatively, tile can sometimes refer to similar units made from lightweight materials such as perlite, wood, and mineral wool, typically used for wall and ceiling applications. In another sense, a tile is a construction tile or similar object, such as rectangular counters used in playing games. The word is derived from the French word tuile, which is, in turn, from the Latin word tegula, meaning a roof tile composed of fired clay, otherwise known as nga."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Alban_chambon%2C_decorazione_in_marmo_e_ceramica%2C_dal_castello_reale_delle_ardenne%2C_houyet%2C_1905_ca._02.jpg/330px-Alban_chambon%2C_decorazione_in_marmo_e_ceramica%2C_dal_castello_reale_delle_ardenne%2C_houyet%2C_1905_ca._02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tile"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?u